        },
        {
          "post_id": "534941",
          "text": "<p>Given the following two files, what will happen when they are compiled and linked together?</p><p><strong>file1.c</strong></p><pre dir=\"ltr\" data-rawcode=\"#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;  static void show() {     printf(&quot;Hello&quot;); }\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"\" data-linenums=\"true\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n\nstatic void show() {\n    printf(\"Hello\");\n}</pre><p><strong>main.c</strong></p><pre dir=\"ltr\" data-rawcode=\"void show();  int main() {     show();     return 0; }\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"\" data-linenums=\"true\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">void show();\n\nint main() {\n    show();\n    return 0;\n}</pre><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\texttt{Hello}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Compilation error<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Linker error<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Runtime error</li></ol>",
